From ccc8f90386c9dd9952b46007cf2c4ad6d6d2d927 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mpaluri <mpaluri@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 21:43:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add SetEndToEndQMDescriptors northbound API for network-level
 QoS

Introduce the SetEndToEndQMDescriptors command at the Network level of
the data model.  The handler resolves each client's serving BSSID,
validates the descriptor, and stores it in the controller database with
source_type=APPLICATION and descriptor_config_type=NETWORK_LEVEL.

A new set_endtoend_qm_descriptor() DB function writes the descriptor
to the EndToEndQMDescriptor DM table (with QMID, ClientMAC, and
DescriptorElement fields), while BSS-level descriptors continue to use
the existing set_qm_descriptor() path.  The DM branch is selected in
set_controller_qm_descriptor() based on descriptor_config_type.

Signed-off-by: Manaswini Paluri <mpaluri@qti.qualcomm.com>

